fact WorkItem(id: "WI-1124", description: some(value: "anthill-todo: `help <command>` — per-command help, rendered from the specs that already describe each command. USER REQUEST 2026-08-17, and it came from being bitten: `anthill-todo migrate` printed 'project already up to date' while workitems.anthill was still one shared file, because TWO different commands share the name `migrate` -- the bundle's WI-434 SCHEMA stamp (StoreFormat version) and WI-1118's LAYOUT move (`migrate --to item-per-file`). Top-level `--help` lists one-line descriptions and nothing else, so there was nowhere to discover the difference. (The immediate message was fixed inline in the same change that filed this; the missing capability is this ticket.)\n\nMOST OF THE DATA ALREADY EXISTS, which is why this is a rendering job and not a documentation project. `anthill.cli.spec` (stdlib/anthill/cli/spec.anthill) declares `OperationSpec(name, description, params: List[ParamSpec], parent)` and `ParamSpec(name, kind, required, description)`, where ParamKind is positional / flag / repeated / bool_flag. The registry in main.anthill builds 24 specs. So `help <command>` is: find the spec by name, print its description, then one line per param -- spelling positional as `<name>` and flag as `--name VALUE`, marking required, and printing each param's own description. No new per-command prose has to be invented for the 16 commands built through the richer spec_* helpers.\n\nTHE GAPS, and they are the actual work:\n  (1) EIGHT commands are built with `spec_named(name, description)`, which passes `params: nil()`. Their help would render a description and no arguments -- which for `list`, `next`, `status` is correct and for others is a silent under-report. Audit the eight and fill in real params rather than shipping empty ones; an argument that exists and is undocumented is worse than no help.\n  (2) TWO commands are HOST-SERVED and are not in the bundle's spec model at all: `fsck` (WI-1114) and `migrate --to` (WI-1118). Both already carry hand-written usage constants in main.rs (FSCK_USAGE, MIGRATE_USAGE) reachable only via `<cmd> --help`. `help <cmd>` must reach those too, or it will confidently report less than `--help` does for exactly the two commands that most needed explaining. Either lift them into OperationSpecs the bundle registers, or have the host intercept `help fsck`/`help migrate`. The first is better and is the reason to prefer it over just adding more `--help` arms.\n  (3) DECIDE whether `help <cmd>` and `<cmd> --help` are the same output. They should be, and one of them should delegate. Today `--help` works for the two host-served commands only, and is swallowed as an argument-error for the other 22.\n\nALSO WORTH DOING while in here: top-level `--help` could mark which commands take arguments, so the list itself hints where `help <cmd>` is worth asking.\n\nAcceptance: a test that DRIVES it -- run `help <cmd>` for a spec'd command and assert the rendered params appear (not merely that it exits 0), and run it for `migrate` and assert BOTH the schema-stamp form and the `--to item-per-file` form are described, since that ambiguity is what filed this ticket. Assert an unknown command name is a loud error naming the closest matches rather than silence."), acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test")], depends_on: some(value: nil), status: Open)
